+## 6. Dated supplement — acknowledgement of the red-team addendum
+
+The red-team amended its file after my response: commit `abcfae7629896126d7c2a19625ff76d2e43ef3f3`
+(2026-11-07T23:41:53Z), adding §9 "two contradictory ballot instructions". I
+read it and reproduced its new claims; **none of it changes my position, and
+several of its points are already conceded above.**
+
+- **9.1 two instructions** — already conceded in my §2 (items 1 and 5) and §3
+  (O1, O2): `a883529` binds `ae39df45…`; `ca73e09` binds `647449cc…`, 20 seconds
+  before the tally commit `3f0b667`. My response reached this independently
+  before reading the addendum. The addendum is correct that the nine later rows
+  were recorded **under the later instruction**, not as transcription drift
+  against the earlier one; my §1 concession says the same.
+- **9.2 §3.2 indeterminacy** — conceded in O6: I cannot define "binding defect"
+  safely when the instructions themselves conflict, which is why the definition
+  is withdrawn rather than repaired.
+- **9.2 §11 sets the earlier instruction** — conceded in O9. §11 is withdrawn as
+  outcome-first and, as the addendum adds, it would have selected the *earlier*
+  of two conflicting instructions against the one under which nine votes were
+  recorded. That makes it worse than I originally conceded, not better.
+- **9.2 provenance of the nine rows** — confirmed independently here, and I add
+  the measurement: `git log --all --diff-filter=A --name-only -- 'records/ballots/executive-innovation-office-act-*.json'`
+  returns **only** `…-c1a00004.json` (`df9a39e`). No individual ballot record for
+  the other nine seats exists in history, and on current `main` only the TSV and
+  the two instruction files exist. So the nine votes rest on a consolidated TSV
+  alone, which does not satisfy the individual-attributability premise of Act 1
+  §2 on its own. This is a further reason no erratum over that record is safe.
+
+**Bottom line unchanged: the bill is withdrawn and must not be enacted.** The
+red-team's §6 alternatives remain the better path, in the order I recommended:
+a new non-protected `records/` errata note that records both instructions and the
+post-enactment merge without editing any ballot; then, if desired, a prospective
+`tests/` change binding ballots to the blob at the tally commit named in the
+enactment record.
+
+Non-claims unchanged: no enactment, no ballot solicited, no protected record
+edited, and no claim that any delivery is unblocked.
